For foreign students, Chinese is a very basic condition for their smooth learning in China’s universities. This compulsory course will help them adapt gradually to the learning requirement of many other courses and become a qualified PKU student.
The aims of the course are:
1. to enhance students’ understanding and using of Chinese research materials through reading the selected materials from newspapers and magazines;
2. to increase students’ professional knowledge and improve their ability of understanding historical and realistic Chinese and international issues with applying to the theories of international politics and diplomacy, as the selected materials are mostly related to international issues;
3. to increase students’ skills of writing and oral expression.

详细信息.教学大纲:
By the time students complete the seminar, they should:
1) Be capable of formulating research questions;
2) Possess proficiency in utilizing academic research databases;
3) Show an understanding of how to analyze data to reach conclusions;
4) Grasp the key tenets of academic writing and presentations;
5) Be familiar with proper citation of academic work;
6) Understand how to plan and organize research;
7) Be able to make a conclusion based on research evidence.

Section 1: Lectures (12 meetings)
Topics cover the entire process of thesis, including selection of research field, raising research questions, hypothesis development, literature review, data collection, data visualization, and basic statistical methods. Students will have hands-on experiences in small tasks in each meeting.

Section 2: student presentation (6 meetings)

Students present progress in 15—20 minutes; faculties in related areas comment.

This course will use a combination of lectures and students presentation.

During the term, the students (working individually and in groups) will be evaluated based on their performance in each of the following activities:
Participation 30%
Assignments 30%
Final presentation 40%

