This course is a theory-practice integrated program designed for senior students in the School of Engineering with a background in biological sciences. The aim of the course is to enable students to understand the main sources of signals in biomedicine, detection methods, and imaging technologies. Through the integration of theory and practice, students will master the fundamental mechanisms and principles as well as the design and operation of basic equipment.
The main content and teaching methods include:
1. Lectures on the fundamental principles of signal generation, detection, and imaging;
2. Hands-on construction of functional systems such as signal detection circuits and assembled microscopes;
3. Acquisition and imaging of actual signals；
4. AI-assisted system design, control and data analysis

