This is a required course for undergraduates at School of news and communication. The main purpose is to introduce the basic principles regarding to the communication ethics and regulations in China. With the completion of the course, the students are expected to acquire the common knowledge of the area and have a healthy and professional view on communication ethics and regulations. Specifically, the course will focus on,
1. The historical, social and institutional prerequisites to the formation of communication ethics and regulations in China;
2. The basic principles of communication ethics and regulations in China;
3. The current practice of communication ethics and regulations in China;
4. Improvements to make to the current communication ethics and regulations in China.

Media play important roles in mediating information and communication processes in social development and social changes. They have profoundly shaped the social, cultural, political, economic, and entertainment aspects of human behaviours. The course is rooted based on fundamental theories in communication, information, and sociology. It systematically overviews the historical changes and current relationships between media and society. The course will focus specifically on the interactions between media and society in the information society. The course objectives include:
1. To help undergraduate students in year 1 or 2 understand the production, organization, public participation of media, and familiarise students with the technical background and content ecology of new media environment;
2. To clarify how different types of media have yielded various impacts on the society, and systematically analyse the influence of media in filtering and gatekeeping information, forming and maintaining social networks, influencing economic lives and technological innovations;
3. To compare the differentiated interactions between media and society in developing and developed countries, especially under the background of globalization, and reflect on the contrast of localization and globalization under the background of the rising impact of transnational technology platforms;
4. To analyse key issues in the frontiers of research in media and society and to grasp important areas in empirically examining the relationship between media and society.

The course aims to train future scientists and management personnel with environmental consciousness, enable them to obtain scientific knowledge about resources, materials and environment, and build up new concepts, standards and life consciousness. We hope the students are able to solve problems from the perspective of environmental protection and make scientific decisions from the long-term interests of human society in their future work and life. Environmental materials involve all activities of human beings, relating to environmental awareness, evaluation of materials and life style choices. Only by raising all people’s environmental awareness and establishing a scientific consumption concept in harmony with nature, can it be possible for the sustainable development of materials.

The course talks about environmental impact of the whole life throughout production, processing, use, disposal from a new perspective, and how to reduce environmental load by evaluation, design and selection of materials. Specific contents of this courses are listed below:
1) basic concepts of sustainable development, requirements for environmental protection and material development;
2) Relationship between material application, development and contemporary global environmental problems;
3) The cause of contemporary hot issues, control strategies and actions of implementing environmental conventions;
4) Analysis of material environmental load;
5) The general tool for environmental management-Life cycle assessment and its application examples in material evaluation;
6) Basic ideas of material recycling design and important role on mitigating environmental load; evaluation and applications of materials with the lowest environmental load.

Over the past decade, the rapid development and widespread application of artificial intelligence, particularly the remarkable performance of large language models like ChatGPT and DeepSeek, have held significant implications for education. As university students, it is essential to stay informed about the latest advancements in AI and learn how to effectively collaborate with these technologies in their studies, laying a solid foundation in AI for future careers.

This course primarily utilizes large language models such as DeepSeek as key technical tools, offering a comprehensive introduction to the latest achievements in various fields of AI and their innovative applications in educational settings. Through this course, students will learn to leverage large language models and other traditional AI technologies (such as data mining, pattern recognition, robotics, etc.) to:

(1) Study efficiently and enhance self-improvement;
(2) Create multimedia courseware to explain knowledge;
(3) Design personalized assignments to understand and evaluate students;
(4) Diagnose learning and teaching conditions;
(5) Provide tailored instruction based on individual needs;
(6) Implement programming and interdisciplinary STEM education.
